-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words: a flat negative, "only", an "if", "where" or
--                "unless" read as the text's no, or a definition that says "is" or "means".
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer: "includes", a scope with no "only", a manner, or silence.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.  O 3 r 2(1) is not threaded.

